  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "certificate",
      "title": "Server-token setup",
      "items": [
        "The operator uploads the public certificate and imports the encrypted .p7m server token. The retained private key decrypts the OAuth credentials; this is separate from an MDM push certificate.",
        "Validation occurs before a locked commit. Ordinary imports reject an established Apple identity or consumer-key change; a concurrent credential or staged-key change rejects the candidate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "service",
      "title": "Recurring reconciliation",
      "items": [
        "Inventory starts with a full fetch, then follows incremental cursors. Invalid or expired cursors restart a fetch. Only successful completion of the current generation reconciles missing devices.",
        "Sync and assignment have independent schedules. Assignment saves outcomes and readback only while account identity, credentials, lease and desired profile still match. Defining a profile also rechecks the account after Apple responds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "warning",
      "title": "Retry and concurrency",
      "items": [
        "HTTP 429 and per-device THROTTLED results defer assignments. A still-owned lease preserves cooldowns across same-identity credential renewal or a changed desired profile, even when its business result is stale.",
        "An identity reset or lost lease rejects old cooldown writes. Account and cursor checks reject stale inventory pages; each accepted page commits atomically with its cursor.",
        "A local conflict stops further batches; it cannot undo work already accepted by Apple. Later runs reconcile the resulting Apple state."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "storage",
      "title": "Explicit identity replacement",
      "items": [
        "Force resets state only for an actual identity change with a validated server UUID. The transaction clears old inventory, profile definitions, target, sessions and retry state, and starts a fresh fetch generation.",
        "The account name, protocol version, creation time and token keypairs survive. Same-identity renewals preserve inventory and target; omitted identity metadata does not erase an established binding.",
        "SQL schema 3 locks a stable account-name row, including absent names and delete/recreate transitions. Custom stores must provide the same transaction-long LockAccount contract."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "transport",
